Footnote extraction is disabled: actual ancillary footnote text must be excluded, while main reading remains. This is an ownership audit, not a request to create citation/ref objects or validate their internal indices. Printed reference marks and their explanatory definitions remain evidence of a source's role even when no citation objects exist.

Locate this exact source in the complete three-page local_raw_evidence. Judge its printed function using raw text, source order and column geometry. OCR classes, preliminary ownership and other model questions are not answers. Do not proofread wording, reconstruct missing OCR text or judge paragraph joins here.

Main reading includes narrative, headings, quotations, exercises, autonomous commentary/endnotes, bibliographies and author/editor signatures attached to a reading section. Running headers, page numbers, publisher directions and actual ancillary footnotes do not belong in it.

A footnote is an auxiliary reading stream attached to continuing main text. Positive evidence can combine a printed mark in the main text, a corresponding explanatory opening and a separate note region in the same local evidence. A literal note mark in mathematics-style delimiters is still a printed mark, not automatically a formula or an ordinary numbered exercise. Do not ignore this relationship merely because the OCR called both sources body.

A footnote can occupy much of a page and contain several natural paragraphs, quotations or an unnumbered continuation. Judge each source within that actual region. A complete sentence or missing repeated number does not turn a demonstrated note continuation into main reading. Conversely an ordinary paragraph near a note remains main text unless its own ancillary role is established.

An autonomous commentary/endnote section begins in the main reading sequence after a discussion has ended, sometimes in the next column on the same page. Its explanations and reference numbers do not make it a footer stream. A bibliography, closing author signature and then a separate headed commentary can be successive main reading sections. Determine the actual column sequence, not the fraction of the page below a box. A heading alone cannot convert notes underneath continuing prose into autonomous commentary.

Position, type size, digits, initials or explanatory genre alone are insufficient. A source mixing genuine main prose with note text must not be excluded wholesale. Only a definite whole-source role contradiction warrants correction; mere uncertainty or a plausible alternative is acceptable.

If the source is retained as paragraph, reject only a demonstrated excluded role. If it is ignored, require restoration only when its main-reading role is established. Do not require deleting reference characters from main text or inventing a missing reference system.

